<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hernandarias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1561">1561</a>–1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Hernando Arias de Saavedra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hernandarias, Hernando Arias de Saavedra, was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a> and was the first American-born governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, holding office several times between 1592 and 1618. He explored the interior, promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> ranching and invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> to found missions among the Guaraní. He proposed the 1617 division of the province into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">governorates</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hernandarias.jpg" alt="Hernandarias" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agus ferrocarril · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Busto_de_Hernandarias_-_Villa_Hernandarias,_Entre_R%C3%ADos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
